  "text": "Pet Cancer Care & Oncology | Broadleys Veterinary Hospital\nSkip to content\nStirling: 01786 445665\nDunblane: 01786 824400\nreception@broadleysvets.co.uk\nEmergency Call\nRepeat Prescriptions\nBroadleys\nVeterinary Hospital\nHome\nAbout\nClose About\nOpen About\nWhy Choose Broadleys\nMeet the Team\nVeterinary Nurses\nPractices\nOut of Hours\nCharity Work\nYour Pets Health\nClose Your Pets Health\nOpen Your Pets Health\nNew Pets, Puppies & Kittens\nID Chips\nDrug Data Sheets\nYour Pet’s Operation\nSenior Pets\nEnd of Life Care\nPreventative Care\nClose Preventative Care\nOpen Preventative Care\nHealth Plans\nOur Health Plan helps you stay on top of your pet’s care, offering gold-standard preventative support.\nRead more\nNeutering\nNeutering prevents unwanted litters and supports long-term health by reducing the risk of serious reproductive issues\nRead more\nVaccinations\nProtect your pet from serious infectious disease by vaccination followed by annual boosters.\nRead more\nParasite Control\nParasite control prevents and treats infections, ensuring your pet stays healthy and happy.\nRead more\nClient Information\nClose Client Information\nOpen Client Information\nHome Deliveries\nPatient Transport\nPet Insurance\nPet Travel Scheme\nPrice List\nRepeat Prescriptions\nReferral Services\nClose Referral Services\nOpen Referral Services\nOrthopaedics\nExpert orthopaedic care restores mobility and improves your pet's quality of life.\nRead more\nPain Management\nPain management techniques enhance your pet's comfort and overall quality of life\nRead more\nNeurology\nNeurology care treats brain, spinal, and nerve disorders, enhancing your pet's well-being\nRead more\nPhysiotherapy & Hydrotherapy\nPromoting healing, improve mobility, and support your pet's recovery.\nRead more\nCardiology\nCardiology services monitor and treat heart conditions, ensuring your pet's health.\nRead more\nOphthalmology\nOphthalmology services provide care for pets, treating complex eye conditions with state-of-the-art techniques.\nRead more\nCT Service\nOur CT service provides detailed imaging for accurate diagnosis and planning\nRead more\nOncology\nOncology services offer comprehensive cancer care, focusing on diagnosis, treatment, and supportive therapy\nRead more\nContact\nBroadleys\nVeterinary Hospital\nMENU\nHome\nAbout\nWhy Chose Broadleys\nMeet the Team\nVeterinary Nurses\nPractices\nOut of Hours Services\nCharity Work\nYour Pets Health\nNew Pets, Puppies & Kittens\nID Chips\nYour Pet’s Operation\nSenior Pets\nTime to say goodbye\nPreventative Care\nHealth Plans\nVaccinations\nNeutering\nParasite Control\nClient Information\nHome Deliveries\nPatient Transport\nPet Insurance\nTaking Your Pet Abroad\nPrice List\nRepeat Prescriptions\nReferral Services\nOrthopaedics\nNeurology\nCardiology\nCT Service\nPhysiotherapy and Hydrotherapy\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nPain Management\nContact Us\nHome\nAbout\nWhy Chose Broadleys\nMeet the Team\nVeterinary Nurses\nPractices\nOut of Hours Services\nCharity Work\nYour Pets Health\nNew Pets, Puppies & Kittens\nID Chips\nYour Pet’s Operation\nSenior Pets\nTime to say goodbye\nPreventative Care\nHealth Plans\nVaccinations\nNeutering\nParasite Control\nClient Information\nHome Deliveries\nPatient Transport\nPet Insurance\nTaking Your Pet Abroad\nPrice List\nRepeat Prescriptions\nReferral Services\nOrthopaedics\nNeurology\nCardiology\nCT Service\nPhysiotherapy and Hydrotherapy\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nPain Management\nContact Us\nIndividually tailored oncology referral service\nOncology\nClare Knottenbelt BVSC MSC DSAM MRCVS, RCVS Recognised specialist in Small Animal Medicine provides oncology referral services at Broadleys veterinary hospital.\nClare worked as a clinician at the University of Glasgow from 2000 and was awarded a Professorship in Small Animal Medicine and Oncology in 2010.\nShe was Clinical Director of the University of Glasgow’s Small Animal Hospital for 6 years and worked within the University’s Oncology service for 11 years before leaving to establish Hawk and Dove.\nFollowing a diagnosis of cancer in your pet, your vet can arrange a consultation with Clare. As well as being an expert in her field, Clare is compassionate and kind.\nShe will discuss all possible care options so that together you can create the most appropriate individual care plan for your pet.\nConsultation options\nFace to face consultations\nare offered at Broadleys Veterinary Hospital\nOnline video consultations\nare also available enabling owners to discuss their pet’s treatment from the comfort of their own home.\nThis option means owners and pets don’t need to travel long distances to seek expert advice but is not suitable for patients with severe clinical symptoms.\nOnline consultations need to be supported by a full clinical examination performed by your own vet prior to the consultation.\nhttps://hawkanddovevets.co.uk/\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hawkanddovevets.co.uk\nHow to contact us\nIf you would like to know more about our oncology at Broadleys Vets, please contact us by email on\nreception@broadleysvets.co.uk\nor call us on\n01786 445665\n(Stirling) or\n01786 824400\n(Dunblane).\nVisit our contact page\nBroadleys\nVeterinary Hospital Limited\nAt Broadleys Veterinary Hospital, our mission is to deliver exceptional, compassionate care, utilising advanced techniques and expertise to enhance the health and well-being of every pet we serve.\nFacebook-f\nInformation\nTime to say goodbye\nHome Deliveries\nID Chips\nPatient Transport\nPet Insurance\nTaking Your Pet Abroad\nYour Pet’s Operation\nPreventative Care\nHealth Plans\nNeutering\nParasite Control\nVaccinations\nSpecialist Care\nOrthopaedics\nNeurology\nCardiology\nPain Management\nHydrotherapy\nPhysiotherapy\nOphthalmology\nOncology\n© 2026 Broadleys Veterinary Hospital Limited\nRegistration Number: SC876273\nRegistered Address: Criaigleith Road, Stirling, FK77LE\nPolicies\nPrivacy Policy\nCookies Policy\nSitemap\nDunblane Premises Update\nThank you to all our clients for their patience during this period of time.\nAs you can expect, it’s been a shock to lose our clinic at Station Road and we are working hard behind the scenes to secure a new location.\nWe have full intentions of staying in Dunblane and are in stages of agreeing a lease. We will use the website and Facebook to keep clients informed of next steps.\nFor all appointments and prescriptions, please give us a call on\n01786 445665\nand our team in Stirling will happily assist you. We are offering free transport to and from Dunblane if this is required while we do not have a clinic in Dunblane.",
